I'm sorry. Just go. Just go.

261
00:15:00,050 --> 00:15:01,970
I can't. I can't.

262
00:15:07,390 --> 00:15:10,310
So I guess you're next. You ready?

263
00:15:07,390 --> 00:15:10,310
I don't think so.

264
00:15:10,480 --> 00:15:14,150
Oh, you're definitely not. I haven't cried like that in years.

265
00:15:14,310 --> 00:15:16,610
You cried yesterday at the 6:00 news.

266
00:15:16,770 --> 00:15:20,150
That old woman was being scammed by her mechanic.

267
00:15:21,610 --> 00:15:24,780
God, I can't believe she saved me for last.

268
00:15:24,950 --> 00:15:26,700
Why are they taking so long?

269
00:15:26,870 --> 00:15:27,990
I don't know.

270
00:15:28,160 --> 00:15:31,460
But, God, Joey seems to be handling it surprisingly well.

271
00:15:34,960 --> 00:15:37,130
No!

272
00:15:44,890 --> 00:15:47,220
Okay, here we go.

273
00:15:50,430 --> 00:15:53,190
Well...

274
00:15:50,430 --> 00:15:53,190
Yeah.

275
00:15:54,100 --> 00:15:56,360
I think I'm gonna take off.

276
00:15:59,650 --> 00:16:00,690
Huh?

277
00:16:00,860 --> 00:16:05,070
Oh, you guys, this was an amazing night. Thank you so much.

278
00:16:05,240 --> 00:16:06,870
I love you.

279
00:16:07,030 --> 00:16:08,700
Good night.

280
00:16:12,750 --> 00:16:14,420
What?

281
00:16:17,460 --> 00:16:19,840
I don't get a goodbye?

282
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:21,920
Lucky bastard.

283
00:16:29,510 --> 00:16:32,890
Unbelievable. She says goodbye to everyone but me!

284
00:16:33,060 --> 00:16:36,440
Well, maybe she thought that with all of your history, it could be...

285
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:40,860
-...you know, implicit.

286
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:40,860
Well, it needs to be "plicit."

287
00:16:41,020 --> 00:16:44,610
All right, let's think about this. I mean, there's gotta be an explanation.

288
00:16:44,780 --> 00:16:48,780
Did you do anything to make her mad?

289
00:16:44,780 --> 00:16:48,780
No, I don't think so.

290
00:16:48,950 --> 00:16:52,580
You know, maybe she was just really spent from our talk.

291
00:16:52,740 --> 00:16:54,660
It was pretty intense.

292
00:16:52,740 --> 00:16:54,660
Yeah, mine too.

293
00:16:54,830 --> 00:16:56,870
Mine was a humdinger.

294
00:16:54,830 --> 00:16:56,870
Okay!

295
00:16:58,580 --> 00:17:03,960
I mean, don't I deserve anything? I mean, a few tears, a cursory hug?

296
00:17:06,090 --> 00:17:08,470
Not from you!

297
00:17:09,600 --> 00:17:12,470
Ross, if you're this upset, you should go and talk to her.

298
00:17:12,640 --> 00:17:15,100
And say what? You owe me a goodbye?

299
00:17:15,270 --> 00:17:18,690
I mean, he's got more pride than that.

300
00:17:15,270 --> 00:17:18,690
The hell I do!

301
00:17:22,650 --> 00:17:25,030
I don't get a goodbye?

302
00:17:22,650 --> 00:17:25,030
What?

303
00:17:25,190 --> 00:17:29,490
Everyone gets a goodbye but me? What do I gotta do to get a goodbye?

304
00:17:29,660 --> 00:17:32,740
Huh? Be best friends with you? Go out with you?

305
00:17:32,910 --> 00:17:34,330
Have a baby with you?

306
00:17:34,500 --> 00:17:37,040
Oh, wait a minute. Wait a minute! I did all those things!

307
00:17:38,290 --> 00:17:40,420
Ross

308
00:17:38,290 --> 00:17:40,420
Or maybe I'm just not giving you...

309
00:17:40,580 --> 00:17:45,260
...enough credit. Uh, I mean, it is difficult to say goodbye to five people.

310
00:17:45,420 --> 00:17:48,300
Goodbye, goodbye, goodbye, goodbye, g--

311
00:17:48,470 --> 00:17:50,300
It's physically impossible!

312
00:17:53,470 --> 00:17:55,890
You know what? After all we've been through...

313
00:17:56,060 --> 00:17:59,310
...I can't believe this is how you want to leave things between us.

314
00:17:59,480 --> 00:18:01,770
Have a good time in Paris.

315
00:18:06,860 --> 00:18:10,070
I hope Ross isn't too upset.

316
00:18:06,860 --> 00:18:10,070
I'm sure he's not more bummed out...

317
00:18:10,240 --> 00:18:12,240
-...than I am.

318
00:18:10,240 --> 00:18:12,240
Tell me about it.

319
00:18:12,410 --> 00:18:15,330
Well, you can't say we don't know how to throw a party.

320
00:18:16,290 --> 00:18:18,290
I think I'm gonna head out.

321
00:18:18,750 --> 00:18:23,040
Uh, where do you think you're going?

322
00:18:18,750 --> 00:18:23,040
I thought I was going home to bed...

323
00:18:23,210 --> 00:18:26,260
...but I'm sensing there's something less fun for me to do here.

324
00:18:27,380 --> 00:18:30,180
We're moving in a couple days and we got a lot of packing to do.

325
00:18:30,340 --> 00:18:34,470
It'd be great if you guys could pitch in.

326
00:18:30,340 --> 00:18:34,470
Joey and I can finish up the guest room.

327
00:18:34,640 --> 00:18:36,390
Yeah, good idea.

328
00:18:37,680 --> 00:18:40,100
Oh, no. You and Phoebe are gonna help me in here.

329
00:18:41,560 --> 00:18:43,150
You couldn't be cool.

330
00:18:44,770 --> 00:18:46,440
We're gonna start in the kitchen.

331
00:18:46,610 --> 00:18:49,650
Plates get put into plate protectors and stacked 10 to a box.

332
00:18:49,820 --> 00:18:53,780
The silverware gets bundled in rubber bands and then bubble wrapped. Got it?

333
00:18:53,950 --> 00:18:55,870
Yeah.

334
00:18:53,950 --> 00:18:55,870
Good. I need you to be careful...

335
00:18:56,030 --> 00:18:58,700
...and efficient. And remember, if I'm harsh with you...

336
00:18:58,870 --> 00:19:01,710
...it is only because you're doing it wrong.

337
00:19:03,830 --> 00:19:06,840
Hey, Mon, I think I figured out whose handcuffs they are.

338
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:09,720
You did? How?

339
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:09,720
Well, I was cleaning out the closet...

340
00:19:09,880 --> 00:19:12,260
...and I found some pictures of them...

341
00:19:12,430 --> 00:19:16,350
-...being used.

342
00:19:12,430 --> 00:19:16,350
Oh, my God, let me see.

343
00:19:18,180 --> 00:19:19,470
Who's that dirty old lady?

344
00:19:21,060 --> 00:19:22,480
Monica's grandmother.

345
00:19:23,980 --> 00:19:27,610
Oh, my God. Nana liked it rough!

346
00:19:29,190 --> 00:19:30,900
Hi.

347
00:19:29,190 --> 00:19:30,900
Hey.

348
00:19:31,070 --> 00:19:32,450
Here, have a seat. Yeah.

349
00:19:32,610 --> 00:19:34,570
How was your night?

350
00:19:32,610 --> 00:19:34,570
Oh, it was okay.

351
00:19:34,740 --> 00:19:37,490
I went to a movie with my cousin then out for dinner.

352
00:19:37,660 --> 00:19:39,620
We went to this place that had--

353
00:19:45,420 --> 00:19:49,000
Anyway, they had these really amazing cheeseburgers.

354
00:19:51,800 --> 00:19:55,050
Erica, are you okay?

355
00:19:51,800 --> 00:19:55,050
Yeah, you know, maybe I ate too much.

356
00:19:55,220 --> 00:19:59,930
I keep getting these stomachaches. They come and go every few minutes.

357
00:20:01,730 --> 00:20:06,150
Oh, my God.

358
00:20:01,730 --> 00:20:06,150
Relax, we'll just get her some antacids.

359
00:20:06,690 --> 00:20:09,190
She doesn't have a stomachache! She's in labor!

360
00:20:09,360 --> 00:20:11,820
Oh, my God!

361
00:20:09,360 --> 00:20:11,820
Yeah, you gotta get to the hospital!

362
00:20:11,990 --> 00:20:15,950
Chandler, get the coats! Erica, let's go! Phoebe and Joey, keep packing!

363
00:20:16,110 --> 00:20:18,660
Oh, my God, we're gonna have a baby.

364
00:20:19,410 --> 00:20:21,200
We're gonna have a baby!

365
00:20:21,370 --> 00:20:23,460
Oh, my God, we're gonna have a baby!

366
00:20:23,620 --> 00:20:26,830
Oh, God, I've gotta sit down! I've gotta sit down!

367
00:20:28,540 --> 00:20:32,090
Honey, it's gonna be okay.

368
00:20:28,540 --> 00:20:32,090
You can do this. Just breathe.

369
00:20:32,510 --> 00:20:35,300
Okay. Okay.

370
00:20:35,470 --> 00:20:36,890
Okay, I feel a little better.

371
00:20:37,050 --> 00:20:40,010
Oh! Are you sure?

372
00:20:41,310 --> 00:20:43,890
Yes, I'm sure. Oh, honey, let's go.

373
00:20:41,310 --> 00:20:43,890
Okay.

374
00:20:44,060 --> 00:20:45,770
Come, let's go.

375
00:20:44,060 --> 00:20:45,770
Bye!

376
00:20:45,940 --> 00:20:47,810
We're having a baby!

377
00:20:45,940 --> 00:20:47,810
Good luck!

378
00:20:47,980 --> 00:20:49,770
Chandler, wait, wait, wait!

379
00:20:47,980 --> 00:20:49,770
What?

380
00:20:49,940 --> 00:20:53,440
If you get a second, find out where she got that cheeseburger.

381
00:21:00,990 --> 00:21:03,950
You think I didn't say goodbye to you because I don't care?

382
00:21:04,120 --> 00:21:05,660
That's what it seemed like.

383
00:21:05,830 --> 00:21:10,540
I cannot believe that after 10 years you do not know one thing about me!

384
00:21:10,710 --> 00:21:16,010
Then why didn't you say something?

385
00:21:10,710 --> 00:21:16,010
Because it is too damn hard, Ross!

386
00:21:16,170 --> 00:21:20,800
I can't even begin to explain to you how much I am gonna miss you.

387
00:21:21,430 --> 00:21:25,640
When I think about not seeing you every day, it makes me not want to go.

388
00:21:26,690 --> 00:21:29,600
Okay? So if you think that I didn't say goodbye to you...

389
00:21:29,770 --> 00:21:33,570
...because you don't mean as much to me as everybody else, you're wrong.

390
00:21:33,730 --> 00:21:36,490
It's because you mean more to me.

391
00:21:36,650 --> 00:21:39,110
So there, all right? There's your goodbye!

392
00:21:39,570 --> 00:21:40,990
Rash!

393
00:21:39,570 --> 00:21:40,990
What?

394
00:21:41,160 --> 00:21:43,370
You keep-

395
00:21:41,160 --> 00:21:43,370
You can't

396
00:21:41,160 --> 00:21:43,370
What?

397
00:22:05,770 --> 00:22:07,980
A little more.

398
00:22:05,770 --> 00:22:07,980
Okay.

399
00:22:08,810 --> 00:22:11,310
A little more. A little more.

400
00:22:08,810 --> 00:22:11,310
All right.

401
00:22:12,650 --> 00:22:14,900
Little more.

402
00:22:17,070 --> 00:22:19,740
All right. All right, let's do this.

403
00:22:17,070 --> 00:22:19,740
All right, ready?

404
00:22:19,910 --> 00:22:22,490
Yep. Now give me your best shot.

405
00:22:23,280 --> 00:22:25,580
All right. Here goes.

406
00:22:30,790 --> 00:22:33,000
Doesn't work.

